      <dct:bibliographicCitation>MacLeod, C. M., &amp; Kampe, K. E. (1996). Word frequency effects on recall, recognition, and word fragment completion tests. Journal of Experimental Psychology: Learning Memory and Cognition, 22(1), 132–142. https://doi.org/10.1037/0278-7393.22.1.132</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Popov, V., &amp; Reder, L. (2024). Frequency effects in recognition and recall. In M. J. Kahana &amp; A. D. Wagner (Eds.), The Oxford handbook of memory (pp. 765–796). Oxford University Press. https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190917982.013.27</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Popov, V., &amp; Reder, L. M. (2020). Frequency effects on memory: A resource-limited theory. Psychological Review, 127(1), 1–46. https://doi.org/10.1037/rev0000161</dct:bibliographicCitation>
