      <dct:bibliographicCitation/>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Hurlstone, M. J. (2024). Serial recall. In M. J. Kahana &amp; A. D. Wagner (Eds.), The Oxford Handbook of Human Memory: Foundations and Applications (Vol. 1, pp. 799–830). Cambridge University Press.</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Hurlstone, M. J., Hitch, G. J., &amp; Baddeley, A. D. (2014). Memory for serial order across domains: An overview of the literature and directions for future research. Psychological Bulletin, 140(2), 339–373. https://doi.org/10.1037/a0034221</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Jacobs, J. (1887). Experiments on "prehension". Mind, (45), 75–79. https://www.jstor.org/stable/2246990</dct:bibliographicCitation>
