   <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/P66-MJRRB9G2-B">
      <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2020-09-28</dcterms:created>
      <dct:creator>Frank Arnould</dct:creator>
      <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-07-25</dcterms:modified>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ATNT</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">autobiographical TNT</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A Think/No-think task involving autobiographical memories where subjects are first asked to generate positive and negative memories from word cues, and then to think about some of these memories and not to think about the others.</skos:definition>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Tâche penser/Ne pas penser portant sur des souvenirs autobiographiques dans laquelle les sujets doivent d'abord générer des souvenirs positifs et négatifs à partir de mots-indices, puis penser à une partie de ces souvenirs et ne pas penser aux autres souvenirs.</skos:definition>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">autobiographical think/no-think task</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">tâche penser/ne pas penser autobiographique</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/P66"/>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>FengYing Lu, WenJing Yang, &amp; Jiang Qiu. (2023). Neural bases of motivated forgetting of autobiographical memories. Cognitive Neuroscience, 14(1), 15–24. https://doi.org/10.1080/17588928.2022.2136150</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Noreen, S., &amp; MacLeod, M. D. (2014). To think or not to think, that is the question: Individual differences in suppression and rebound effects in autobiographical memory. Acta Psychologica, 145, 84–97. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actpsy.2013.10.011</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Noreen, S., &amp; MacLeod, M. D. (2013). It’s all in the detail : Intentional forgetting of autobiographical memories using the autobiographical think/no-think task. Journal of Experimental Psychology: Learning, Memory, and Cognition, 39(2), 375‑393. https://doi.org/10.1037/a0028888</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Stephens, E., Braid, A., &amp; Hertel, P. T. (2013). Suppression-induced reduction in the specificity of autobiographical memories. Clinical Psychological Science, 1(2), 163–169. https://doi.org/10.1177/2167702612467773</dct:bibliographicCitation>
