   <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/P66-L0QT15F8-G">
      <dcterms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2017-12-04</dcterms:created>
      <dct:creator>Frank Arnould</dct:creator>
      <dcterms:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-06-07</dcterms:modified>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">inhibition proactive</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">proactive inhibition</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Processus par lequel des souvenirs anciens perturbent la rétention de nouvelles informations.</skos:definition>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process by which older memories disrupt the retention of newer information.</skos:definition>
      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/JVR-H9F96K6T-2"/>
      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/N9J-ZH1LNPNG-D"/>
      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://www.cognitiveatlas.org/concept/id/trm_4a3fd79d0adab"/>
      <skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">inhibitions proactives</skos:hiddenLabel>
      <skos:hiddenLabel xml:lang="fr">interférences proactives</skos:hiddenLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">interférence proactive</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">proactive interference</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.loterre.fr/ark:/67375/P66"/>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Anderson, M. C., &amp; Neely, J. H. (1996). Interference and inhibition in memory retrieval. In E. L. Bjork &amp; R. A. Bjork (Eds.), Memory (p. 237‑313). Academic Press. https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-012102570-0/50010-0</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Bergström, J. A. (1893). Experiments upon physiological memory by means of the interference of associations. The American Journal of Psychology, 5(3), 356–369. https://doi.org/10.2307/1410999</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Keppel, G., &amp; Underwood, B. J. (1962). Proactive inhibition in short-term retention of single items. Journal of Verbal Learning and Verbal Behavior, 1(3), 153‑161. https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5371(62)80023-1</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Kliegl, O., &amp; Bäuml, K.-H. T. (2021). Buildup and release from proactive interference – Cognitive and neural mechanisms. Neuroscience &amp; Biobehavioral Reviews, 120, 264–278. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neubiorev.2020.10.028</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Maslow, A. H. (1934). The effect of varying time intervals between acts of learning with a note on proactive inhibition. Journal of Experimental Psychology, 17(1), 141–144. https://doi.org/10.1037/h0069853</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>MacLeod, C. M. (2024). Interference theory: History and current status. In M. J. Kahana &amp; A. D. Wagner (Eds.), The Oxford handbook of human memory: Foundations and applications (Vol. 2, pp. 1173–1208). Oxford University Press. https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190917982.013.40</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Neath, I., &amp; Surprenant, A. M. (2015). Proactive interference. In J. Wright (Ed.), International Encyclopedia of the Social &amp; Behavioral Sciences (p. 1‑8). Elsevier. https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-097086-8.51054-X</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Underwood, B. J. (1957). Interference and forgetting. Psychological Review, 64(1), 49-60. https://doi.org/10.1037/h0044616</dct:bibliographicCitation>
