      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Kopelman, M. D. (1987). Two types of confabulation. Journal of Neurology, Neurosurgery &amp; Psychiatry, 50(11), 1482–1487. https://doi.org/10.1136/jnnp.50.11.1482</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>La Corte, V., Serra, M., Attali, E., Boissé, M.-F., &amp; Barba, G. D. (2010). Confabulation in Alzheimer’s disease and amnesia: A qualitative account and a new taxonomy. Journal of the International Neuropsychological Society, 16(6), 967–974. https://doi.org/10.1017/S1355617710001001</dct:bibliographicCitation>
      <dct:bibliographicCitation>Moscovitch, M. (1997). Strategic retrieval and the frontal lobes: Evidence from confabulation and amnesia. Neuropsychologia, 35(7), 1017–1034. https://doi.org/10.1016/S0028-3932(97)00028-6</dct:bibliographicCitation>
